-- title:
--   Crossing presentation of the K-node ring, q ≥ 5
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a natural number $N \neq 0$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$, a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$, modular polynomial data `data` for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \equiv (Y^q - X)(Y - X^q)$ mod $q$, integrality of the two degeneracy maps $\bar\alpha, \bar\beta$ from level $N$ to level $Nq$, a place specialisation $P$ of the places of `modularFunctionFieldBar N` to those of `modularFunctionFieldC k N`, and a prolongation tuple $R$ for $P$ (two regular prolongations $R_1, R_2$ of $A$ to level $Nq$ linked by the Atkin–Lehner involution, together with the residue data). Assume $q \nmid N$ and $5 \le q$; that $R$ satisfies `IsModel` (the two divisor laws at the non-Frobenius-fixed places and the two cusp laws) and `OrderLawFixed` (at an affine place $v$ fixed by the square of the geometric Frobenius, the $\bar\alpha$-pushforward of the divisor of $f$ at $v$ equals $\operatorname{ord}_v$ of the first residue plus $\operatorname{ord}$ of the second residue at the Frobenius image of $v$). Let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC k N`, all supersingular (rational, affine, with $j$-value in the supersingular set `ssJSet q k`), and assume the regularity law and the node-value law of $R$ on $W$. Let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $w \in W$. Write $\mathcal{O} = R.\mathtt{nodeIntegersOver } K\, w$ for the subring of elements of the level-$Nq$ function field integral for $R_1$, for $R_2$ and at every place above $w$ under $\bar\alpha$-reduction, whose Laurent expansion lies in the subfield generated by the constants of $A \cap K$ and the two $j$-series. Assume both node residue maps are saturated: on the first branch, whenever $\operatorname{ord}_w$ of the first residue of $g$ is positive and $\operatorname{ord}_w$ of that of $g'$ is $1$, the first residue of $g$ is the product of that of $g'$ with the first residue of some element of $\mathcal{O}$, and correspondingly on the second branch with $w$ replaced by its arithmetic Frobenius twist. Let $c_0$ be a node-coordinate datum over $K$ at $w$, that is a pair $(x_0, y_0)$ in $\mathcal{O}$ whose first residue vanishes on $x_0$ and has order $1$ at $y_0$, and whose second residue vanishes on $y_0$ and has order $1$ at $x_0$. Finally let $\varpi \in A \cap K$ be such that an element of $A \cap K$ reduces to $0$ under $red$ exactly when it is a multiple of $\varpi$. Then there is a node-coordinate datum $c = (x, y)$ over $K$ at $w$ with $(\varpi, x) = (\varpi, x_0)$ and $(\varpi, y) = (\varpi, y_0)$ as ideals of $\mathcal{O}$ (constants taken via the ring map $R.\mathtt{nodeConst}$), integers $e_K \ge 1$ and $E \ge 1$, a unit $\varepsilon$ of $A \cap K$ with $q = \varpi^{e_K}\varepsilon$, and a unit $u$ of $\mathcal{O}$ with $xy = \varpi^{E} u$, such that $(\varpi, x, y)$ is the unique maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$, both $(\varpi, x)$ and $(\varpi, y)$ are prime, and $y \notin (\varpi, x)$, $x \notin (\varpi, y)$.
--
--   This is the local crossing (node) presentation of the ring of functions of $X_0(Nq)$ over $A \cap K$ at a supersingular point of the special fibre in characteristic $q$: the two branches of the Deligne–Rapoport model cross transversally, with $xy$ a power of the uniformiser times a unit. It is the $q \ge 5$ case of the general crossing-presentation statement and is used in the derivation of the unrestricted version `exists_crossingPresentation_nodeIntegersOver_of_orderLawFixed_of_saturated`.
